Hi Sunthud, Yves and list,

I just realized a mistake I made about the lavaan code. Actually most of the values I specified for the parameters were starting values, not fixed values for the parameters. So instead of the previous code. The improved code should look like this:

popModel="
f1=~start(0.7)*q1+start(0.78)*q2+start(0.65)*q3;f2=~start(0.85)*q4+start(0.85)*q5;
f3=~start(0.79)*q6+start(0.94)*q7+start(0.65)*q8+start(0.76)*q9;f4=~start(0.74)*q10+start(0.64)*q11+start(0.68)*q12;
f1=~start(0.1)*q4+start(0.14)*q5+start(0.24)*q6+start(0.13)*q7+start(0.25)*q8+start(0.32)*q9+start(0.22)*q10+start(0.24)*q11+start(0.21)*q12;
f2=~start(0.1)*q1+start(0.14)*q2+start(0.24)*q3+start(0.13)*q6+start(0.25)*q7+start(0.32)*q8+start(0.22)*q9+start(0.24)*q10+start(0.1)*q11+start(0.21)*q12;
f3=~start(0.1)*q1+start(0.14)*q2+start(0.24)*q3+start(0.13)*q4+start(0.25)*q5+start(0.32)*q10+start(0.22)*q11+start(0.21)*q12;
f4=~start(0.1)*q1+start(0.14)*q2+start(0.24)*q3+start(0.13)*q4+start(0.25)*q5+start(0.32)*q6+start(0.22)*q7+start(0.24)*q8+start(0.1)*q9;
q1~~start(0.4)*q1;q2~~start(0.3)*q2;q3~~start(0.25)*q3;q4~~start(0.5)*q4;q5~~start(0.43)*q5;q6~~start(0.3)*q6;
q7~~start(0.32)*q7;q8~~start(0.28)*q8;q9~~start(0.16)*q9;q10~~start(0.24)*q10;q11~~start(0.17)*q11;q12~~start(0.29)*q12;
f1~~1*f1;f2~~1*f2;f3~~1*f3;f4~~1*f4;
f1~~start(0.35)*f2;f1~~start(0.28)*f3;f1~~start(0.19)*f4;f2~~start(0.38)*f3;f2~~start(0.41)*f4;f3~~start(0.26)*f4
"
analyzeModel="
f1=~start(0.7)*q1+start(0.78)*q2+start(0.65)*q3;f2=~start(0.85)*q4+start(0.85)*q5;
f3=~start(0.79)*q6+start(0.94)*q7+start(0.65)*q8+start(0.76)*q9;f4=~start(0.74)*q10+start(0.64)*q11+start(0.68)*q12;
f1~~1*f1;f2~~1*f2;f3~~1*f3;f4~~1*f4;
f3+f4~f1+f2
"

However, the same error as before happened with the new code. Hopefully this change could help solve this issue to some extent.

I have one further question, is there any simple way to specify the starting values? The way in the above situation feels a little bit repeat.

Best regards,

ya

